// @x is the co-maximal write to x, not the last write in rhb order (#124).
//
// MoRDor's own test. r1 = 1 has thread 2 read x := 1 after its own x := 2, so
// x := 1 is co-after x := 2 and x ends at 1. With r1 = 1, @x = 2 is impossible
// under SC, and under every model with CoWR (r1 fr x := 2 closes hb;fr). rhb
// leaves the two writes unordered, and @x used to be whichever came last in
// it, so MoRDor allowed @x = 2 && r1 = 1. The allows are the outcomes some
// admitted co does end with.
x := 0;
{
  x := 1
} ||| {
  x := 2;
  r1 := x
}
%%
forbid (@x = 2 && r1 = 1) [SC, RC11, OCaml, sMRD]
allow (@x = 1 && r1 = 1) [SC]
allow (@x = 1 && r1 = 2) [SC]
allow (@x = 2 && r1 = 2) [SC]
